cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ArthaBench Pro or its technical reports, please cite it as below."
title: "ArthaBench Pro: Reliability-Focused Financial Intelligence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Shreyash
    affiliation: "Ajeenkya DY Patil University, Pune"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shreyashsinghegi2-oss/artha-bench-pro"
url: "https://artha-bench-pro.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  An educational financial intelligence platform in which deterministic, tested code owns every number
  and language models only explain them. Includes a certified-arithmetic engine (EMI, SIP, CAGR, XIRR,
  bond YTM, Indian income tax) that returns a proven error bound or no number, a grounded A–H advisory
  pipeline with number checking, hybrid retrieval over regulatory text, and a seeded Monte Carlo engine.
keywords:
  - financial AI
  - reliability
  - interval arithmetic
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - India
date-released: "2026-10-01"
